1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Daniel-Lovett/6000000002043298985?through=6000000001081975169
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Unknown-2096
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes married William Swetland. William and Agnes Swetland were probably born prior t.o 1650, and came from England or Sweden. They resided in Salem, Massachusetts, in 1676, and in Salem, New London County, Connecticut, in 1703.[1
2 CONC ] This source recorded four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Peter born September 1, 1676 - No family
2 CONT # Grace born March 8, 1679-80
2 CONT # John born September 1, 1681
2 CONT # Joseph born January 5, 1683
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes died in 1749 in the Massachusetts Bay Colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Footnote entry about William Swetland, without further reference. Transcript follows.
2 CONT
2 CONT “William Swetland, born about 1646, married Agnes. .  she married, secondly, Simon Lovitt of Beverly, Oct 10, 1676: children 1. Peter, born Sept. 1, 1676, 2. Grace, born March 8, 1679-80, John, born Sept. 1, 1681; fisherman, lived
2 CONC  in Marblehead in 1705; 34. Joseph, born Jan. 5, 1683-4. "
2 CONT
2 CONT However, In this 2003 version, the wife of Simon Lovett is shown as the eldest child of William and Agnes (____) Swetland--Agnes, b. 1672 at Beverly, based on "…[convincing] data from Judith Leone Young-Thayer" (see para 4 p. xix"
2 CONC ).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Unknown-2096
