2 CONT
2 CONT 4a. Benjamin. (William (p. 1), John, Isaac) Married Mrs. Hannah Hale of Boston, MA, at Lynn, MA, on September 1.1, 1707. Settled at New London, CT. They had no children. He was a man who was well informed and left a large estate. 
2 CONC In 17218 he subscribed to the "Prince's Chronology", and it is said that those upon that list were considered as the Priciple Literati of New England. He owned land in New London and Hartford counties, and two negroes, besides oth
2 CONC er property. Left an estate of over 1,000 pounds and two negroes. A major court controversy ensued between the widow and the executor.
