1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Patriot of the American Revolution service MA,  Rank Lieutenant DAR Ancestor # A007244 Service Source:  MA SOLS & SAILS, VOL 1, P 760 Service Description:  1) 1LT; CAPTS EDWARD COBB, JOSEPH KEITH, ABRAM WASHBURN; 2
2 CONC ) MAJ ELIPHALET CAREY; COLS TITCOMB, COTTON
2 CONT
2 CONT Find A Grave Memorial # 43917446 http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=43917446
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bassett-1923
2 CONT
2 CONT Lt. Joseph Bassett Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 2 Mar 1731 in Bridgewater, Plymouth, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Joseph Bassett and Elisabeth (Ames) Bassett
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Dorothy (Bassett) Packard and Sarah (Bassett) Dyer
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Phebe (Cushman) Bassett — married 2 Dec 1756 in Bridgewater, Plymouth, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Sarah (Prior) Bassett — married 14 Jan 1798 in Bridgewater, Plymouth, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Caleb Bassett, Phebe (Bassett) Leonard, Nathan Bassett, Abigail (Bassett) Lathrop, Joseph Bassett III, Hannah (Bassett) Alger, David Bassett and Cushman Bassett
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 6 May 1803 in Bridgewater, Plymouth, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 16 Sep 2019 | Created 5 Jan 2015
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Plymouth Colony and Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT From John Maltby: Joseph and Elisabeth (Ames) Bassett had children,[1] including: Lt. Joseph Bassett (Jr.), born on 2 Mar. 1730/1 in Bridgewater,[2] married as his 1st wife:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.) Phebe Cushman, daughter of Jabez and Sarah (Paddleford) Cushman,[3] on 2 Dec. 1756 in Bridgewater.[4] She was born ca. 1737,[5] a granddaughter of Benjamin and Sarah (Eaton) Cushman,[6] and of Jonathan and Hannah (King) Paddle
2 CONC ford.[7] She died on 25 Feb. 1796 in Bridgewater, aged 58 years,[8] and he remarried to:
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.) Sarah (Pri­or) (Fobes) Eaton, daughter of Joseph and Ann (Moore) Prior, and widow of Josiah Fobes (Jr.), of Bridgewater, and of John Eaton, of Greenwich, CT,[9] on 14 Jan. 1798 in Bridgewater.[10] He was living in Bridgewater,
2 CONC  MA, in the 1790 federal census.[11] Lt. Joseph Bassett died testate on 6 May 1803 in Bridgewater, aged 72 years,[12] his will dated 5 Apr. 1798, and probated on 2 June 1803, mentioned his wife Sarah, his five sons Caleb, Nathan, 
2 CONC Joseph, David and Cushman Bassett, and his three daughters Phebe Leonard, Abiel Lathrop, and Hannah Alger, and he named his son Caleb Bassett as executor of his estate.[13] (See Appendix (A) for a full transcription of his will.)
2 CONT
2 CONT He had had children by Phebe Cushman:[14] Caleb Bassett, born on 11 Nov. 1757 in Bridgewater, married Bethiah Keith, daughter of Benjamin and Abigail (Leach) Keith, of Bridgewater, on 18 Apr. 1782 in Bridgewater, and they settled 
2 CONC in New Gloucester, ME. Phebe Bassett, born on 19 Aug. 1759 in Bridgewater, married Barnabas “Barney” Leonard, of Taunton, MA, on 5 Feb. 1780 in Bridgewater. She died on 30 Oct. 1838 in Bridgewater, aged 79 years. Nathan Bassett, b
2 CONC orn on 12 Aug. 1763 in Bridgewater, settled in Genesee, NY. Abigail Bassett, born on 12 Sept. 1765 in Bridgewater, married Seth Lathrop (Jr.), son of Seth and Mehitabel (Daily) Lathrop, on 25 Nov. 1784 in Bridgewater. Joseph Basse
2 CONC tt (3rd), born on 5 Jan. 1769 in Bridgewater, married Ruth Leach, daughter of James and Hasadiah (Keith) Leach, on 26 Jan. 1792 in Bridgewater. Hannah Bassett, born on 8 June 1771 in Bridgewater, married Deacon James Alger Jr., so
2 CONC n of James and Martha (Kingman) Alger, of Bridgewater, on 29 May 1791 in Bridgewater. She died a widow on 16 Jan. 1845 in Bridgewater, aged 73 years, of old age. David Bassett, married Phebe Dean, daughter of Job and Judith (Willi
2 CONC ams) Dean, of Raynham, MA, on 15 Dec. 1796 in Raynham, and they settled in Maine. Rev. Cushman Bassett, also settled in Maine. Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Mitchell, History of Bridgewater, p. 112, says they had Dorothy 1726, Joseph 1731, and Sarah 1734. ↑ Bridgewater VRs, Vol. 1, p. 42. ↑ Van Antwerp, Lee Douglas, and Robert S. Wakefield, Mayflower Families Through Five Generation
2 CONC s, Volume Nine, Family of Francis Eaton, General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 1996, [hereinafter MF5G: Eaton], p. 104; Vital Records of Taunton, Massachusetts, To the Year 1850, New England Historic Genealogical Society, Bost
2 CONC on, 1929, [hereinafter Taunton VRs], Vol. 2, p. 132, marriage of Jabez Cushman, of Plympton, and Sarah Paddleford, of Taunton, on 2 Dec. 1736 in Taunton. ↑ Bridgewater VRs, Vol. 2, p. 43. ↑ Calculated from her age at death. ↑ MF5G
2 CONC : Eaton, p. 33. ↑ MF5G: Eaton, p. 104. ↑ Bridgewater VRs, Vol. 2, p. 435. ↑ Mitchell, History of Bridgewater, pp. 112, 160, 280. ↑ Bridgewater VRs, Vol. 2, p. 43. ↑ Heads of Families at the First Census of the United States Taken 
2 CONC in the Year 1790: Massachusetts, Bountiful, Utah, 1993, p. 166, Bridgewater Town, Plymouth County, the Joseph Bassett household had 3 free white males aged 16 or older, 1 free white male under 16, and 2 free white females. ↑ Bridg
2 CONC ewater VRs, Vol. 2, p. 434, buried in Scotland Graveyard in Bridgewater. ↑ Plymouth County Probate Docket #1436, Vol. 38, p. 327-328, from FHL microfilm #0550720. ↑ Mitchell, History of Bridgewater, p. 112, says they had Caleb 175
2 CONC 7, Phebe, Nathan 1763, Abigail, Joseph 1769, Hannah 1771, David and Cushman. John A. Maltby Genealogies - Elisabeth Ames - child # 705 [services.dar.org/public/dar_research] A007244 Service: MASSACHUSETTS Rank(s): LIEUTENANT Find 
2 CONC A Grave: Memorial #43917446
