1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ancestor: SEARLE, GIDEON (A101015) - Verified but not entered into the Descendants Listing.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_member/?Action=full&National_Number=167938
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Gideon (1762-1830) is the 1st Cousin of the Gideon Searl (b. 1720) who was appointed with Ebenezer Wallis on October 22, 1762 at Pownal on the New Hampshire Grants to attend the committee, "to lay out the township of Arlington, an
2 CONC d part thereof into lots, that is, two lots to each proprietor's right, one of one acre, and one of one hundred acres", "to make camps, take care of horses and cook."  The Searls' and their families came to inhabit a few log house
2 CONC s in a small clearing North of the present Arlington Village.  On June 1, 1763, the Proprietors held their adjourned meeting at the house of William Searl (b. 1728), brother of Gideon (b. 1720), in one of those log houses.  Gideon
2 CONC 's father John Searl (b. 1711), the brother of Gideon (b. 1720) and William (b. 1728), was appointed Moderator of the Proprietor's Meeting begun on October 22, 1762 and subsequently at that meeting he was appointed an assessor and
2 CONC  a member of the Committee to lay out the Town of Arlington as noted above.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gideon (1762-1830) was the son of Gideon Searl (1742-1798) and his wife Cynthia Sweetland (Swetland) (b. 1742).  Gideon (1742-1798) was the son of John Searl (b. 1711) and his wife Margaret Cook (1722-1776).          
2 CONT
2 CONT A Gideon Searl (either Gideon at the age of 15 years or his father at the age of 35 years) served as a Private, from February 3rd to February 28, 1779, in Captain John Smith's Company in Colonel Gideon Warren's 5th Regiment of Ver
2 CONC mont Militia while they were called out in the service of the State.  About 3 months later on May 12th, a Gideon Searl entered the service as a Private in Captain Thomas Sawyer's Company of Vermont Miltia raised for the defence of
2 CONC  the Northern Fronties.  After serving 1 month and 18 days, he was discharged on June 28, 1779, for which he was paid 3 pounds, 9 shillings and 0 pence.    
2 CONT
2 CONT A Gideon Searl was one of 23 Freeman residing in the Town of Wells, Bennington (now Rutland) County, Vermont in the year 1780.
2 CONT
2 CONT On September 6, 1780, a Gideon Searl entered the service as a Private in Captain Eli Noble's Company in Major Ebenezer Allen's Detachment who were in the service of the State of Vermont from August 16, 1780 to the 21st of November
2 CONC  following, both days included.  During this period, this Gideon was credited with 65 days of service and paid 4 pounds, 6 shillings and 8 pence wages and 7 shellings for 2 days travel.  During this same period of time, another Gi
2 CONC deon Searl, served as a Private for 19 days, marching on October 11th and being discharged on October 29th, in Captain Abel Meriman's (Wells) Company of Colonel Ebenezer Allen's Vermont Militia Regiment for a tour to Castleton.  T
2 CONC his call up of Colonel Allen's Regiment was in response to an alarm caused by the raid led by British Major Christopher Carleton into the Lake Champlain Valley and beyond.     
2 CONT
2 CONT From June 10th to the 11th, 1781, Gideon, Junior and his father served one day with a detachment of men from the Town of Wells in Captain Jacob Wood's (Tinmouth) Company, Colonel Thomas Lee's Regiment for a tour to Castleton. The 
2 CONC Well's detachment came from the portion of the Town of Wells which became a part of Tinmouth in 1784.  In this Company was Captain Wood's 1st Cousin, Corporal Steven Wood, who beame Gideon's next door neighbor in Whitehall, Washin
2 CONC gton County, New York many years later.  A little over a couple of months later, on August 20th, a Gideon Searl commenced service as a Private in Captain George Sexton's Company of Volunteers belonging to Colonel Ebenezer Walbridg
2 CONC e's Regiment raised for the defence of the Frontiers of Vermont.  Captain Sexton's Company marched to Skenesborough, Charlotte County, (after 1786 - Whitehall, Washington County) New York.  After serving 93 day, this Gideon was di
2 CONC scharged on November 20th and paid 6 pounds, 9 shillings and 2 pence for wages and 18 miles travel.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the time of the taking of the 1st US Census in 1790, Gideon Searls, Junr. was enumerated as the Head of a Household residing in Whitehall, Washington County, New York with 2 males of 16 years of age and older, 2 males under the
2 CONC  age of 16 years and 4 females.  Gideon's father was also enumerated as the Head of a Household residing in Whitehall at that time with 2 males of 16 years of age and older, 1 male under the age of 16 years and 3 females.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gideon (1762-1830) married for his 1st Wife Hannah Woodward (1768-1811) and later Lucy Squire (1784-1834) by whom he collectively had 14 children (7 sons and 7 daughters): Abraham (1787-1846), Isaac (1789-1860), Phebe (Pheobe) (17
2 CONC 91-1869), Jacob, Samuel (1796-1874), Parmella, Arza (b. 1802), Marilla, Cynthia, Gideon, Daniel, Hannah (1815-1884), Lucy and Emily,                   
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) "The Vermont Historical Gazetteer: A Magazine, embracing A History of Each Town, Civil, Ecclesiastical, Biographical and Military." Vol. 1. Addison, Bennington, Caledonia, Chittenden and Essex Counties, by Abby Maria Hemenway,
2 CONC  pages 122 and 123
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) "The History of Ancient Windsor, Connecticut," by Henry R. Stiles, 1859, page 770
2 CONT
2 CONT (3) "History of Rutland County Vermont with Illustrations and Biographical Sketches of Some of its Prominent Men and Pioneers" by H. P. Smith and W. S. Rann, 1886, page 848
2 CONT
2 CONT (4) "The State of Vermont Rolls of the Soldiers in the Revolutionary War 1775 to 1783" by John E. Goodrich, 1904, pages 16-17, 105-106, 123-125, 203-205, 208-209, 381-382 and 552-553
2 CONT
2 CONT (5) Washington County, New York Surrogate Court Records, Will Book A1, page 159, and Book A2, page 500* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/21459813/gideon-searl Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/
2 CONC SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 27 2022, 18:51:56 UTC''
