1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "His brother Jacob was quite a popular hotel keeper. His hotel was in Wachogue what is  now one of the streets of Springfield. When he was a young man he  went courting a girl named Annie Jennings. Jacol) being a p
2 CONC oor boy, her  stepfather was opposed to his calling to see Annie. He called at one time  and this stepfather told him he must go and as Jacob rose to leave, Annie  also arose and said if Jacob goes, I go with him. They went that d
2 CONC ay in  1813 and were married. Thus they started in life without money or home.  By hard work and economy he accumulated quite a fortune for those  times, estimated about §20,000. He had no education and could neither  read nor wri
2 CONC te. They had one child Belinda. They educated her and she  became quite a smart woman. She married David Eaton and they had 12  children, some of whom are living at the present time." from 1st annual Swetland Family Reunion (1896)
