1 NAME Elizabeth /Brown/
2 GIVN Elizabeth
2 SURN Brown
2 _MARNM Bowen
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1 JUL 1785
2 PLAC New York, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 JUL 1875
2 PLAC Bertie, Welland, Ontario, Canada
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bruce C. Johnson Jr. Research notes 1985 - 1995
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: Husband was William BOWEN not "Bower" 
2 CONT
2 CONT Will dated 11 June 1861; probated at Welland Co., Ont., 13 July 1876; Application 702, Grant #682; FHL film #580600; and FHL film #1428011, p. 470, Probate name given in error as Elizabeth Brown; son William Bowen, executor. She b
2 CONC equeathed $50 to her Grandson Michael Bowen and the remainder to her son William Bowen. The probate record indicates that she died 8 July 1875.
2 CONT
2 CONT   Elizabeth was born January 1, 1786 in New York. According to Violetta Brown's Revolutionary War Pension application filed in 1857 by Walter Brown, Elizabeth married William Bowen in 1800. 
2 CONT
2 CONT    They settled near Fort Erie and had seven sons and four daughters: William, Henry, Polly, Robert, Nelson, John, Hannah, Walter, Clarissa, Edward, and Barbara. Willam Sr. died 26 Mar 1860 and Elizabeth died 8 July 1875. They are
2 CONC  both buried at Fort Erie.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1872 Atlas of Welland shows a William Bowen living on Conc. 5 next to a Robert Bowen just south of the Canada Southern and Glencoe Loop Line.
2 CONT
2 CONT    Welland Co. death notices for Ft. Erie [Ontario Register] give Elizabeth, wife of William Bowen, died 8 July 1875, age 90 years, 6 months and 8 days
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas Carter Brown diary (NCB was a nephew to Elizabeth. He was son of Elizabeth's brother Walter Brown of Malahide Twp.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 August 1874, "To Aunt Elizabeth Bowen. 90 feeble. (NCB Diary.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT    Notices in Niagara, died 15 July 1875, age 90 yrs, 6mo. & 8 dys.
