2 CONT Page 4, The Medina County Gazette, Medina, Ohio, Friday, September 17th, 1886
2 CONT Another of our pioneers is gone, Geo. A. Phelps died on Monday last, aged 82 years. He leaves a wife, two sons and two daughters , all of whom were in attendance to administer to his wants during his sickness. He came from Connect
2 CONC icut in the spring of '35, and located on a piece of land in the then wilderness, and has lived on the same farm for 51 years. He passed peacefully away.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biographical and ahistorical data on People & Events of Brunswick, Medina County, Ohio, From Notes of Winifred Wolcott, Cincinnati, Ohio, Typed by the Genealogical Society, Salt Lake City, Utah, 1962
2 CONT Page 45
2 CONT Mr. & Mrs. George Phelps moved from Con. to Brunswick, O., with a three horse team, 23 days on the road. They lived to celebrate their golden wedding at which time she told of walking to Hinckley and exchanging Palm Leaf hats (whi
2 CONC ch she had braided) for a four gallon churn which she took under her arm and walked home. Making a walk of eight miles. She passed around for inspection some of her wedding garments spun, woven and made by her own hands.
