1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/42722996/person/342113027728 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 21 2019, 15:58:59 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Eleazer Densmore and Phebe Searle.
2 CONT Husband of Ann Maria Webster, married 1854.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn86061216/1918-02-05/ed-1/seq-4/
2 CONT
2 CONT PIONEER CITIZEN PASSES
2 CONT Edgewood, Feb. 1 – Anson Densmore, a pioneer citizen of Edgewood, 90 years of age, died in Long Beach, Cal., last Friday at the hone of his son, F. A. Densmore.  Mr. Densmore is the last member but one of the Octogenarian club of 
2 CONC Edgewood, which was organized February 1, 1907.  The Octogenarian club is the most famous club of its kind, if not the only one in existence in the state of Iowa, composed only of men from 77 years of age or more.
2 CONT
2 CONT Find A Grave contributor Rebecca Sheehan-Plotkin
