1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/42722996/person/342113027930 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 21 2019, 15:58:59 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Edgewood Journal
2 CONT Thursday 31 Mar 1921
2 CONT Mrs. Cynthia Smith is seriously ill at the home of her daughter, Mrs. C.A. Hesner; her son, Lute Smith, has been summoned from Dakota. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edgewood Journal 
2 CONT Thursday 07 Apr 1921
2 CONT Venerable Lady Enters Last Sleep
2 CONT Cynthia Densmore was born in Ischua, New York on July 23, 1933.
2 CONT She was the sister of the late Anson Densmore.
2 CONT On February 9th, 1851, she was united in marriage to Alonzo F. Smith, of Hinsdale, N.Y., the ceremony occurred in ??ce, N.Y.
2 CONT For twelve years after the marriage, Mr. and Mrs. Smith continued to reside in their native state of N.Y.  In the year 1848 (likely should read 1863), the call of the West became so insistent that they obey the impulse and came to
2 CONC  Iowa.  They purchased a farm adjoining the village of Yankee Settlement on the east, where they continued to reside until the death of Mr. Smith, which occurred on the 22nd day of May 1904  The home farm they established has ever
2 CONC  since remained under the control of the family, now being in the possession of their son Charles.  Mrs. Smith has lived to witness many changes in her surroundings.  The railroad entered upon the scene and the humble village of Y
2 CONC ankee Settlement became the thriving town of Edgewood.  She entered upon new scenes and changed conditions and one by one she bids farewell to all of her associates of the pioneer days.  At the time of her death she was said to be
2 CONC  the eldest living member of the M.E. Church of Edgewood, of which organization she had been a faithful member during her residence in Iowa.
2 CONT Only three sons out of a family of seven children are today living to bid an affectionate farewell to a loving mother, whose every thought was welfare of her children.  The ones remaining are Luther F. Smith, of Dell Rapids, S.D.,
2 CONC  Charles A. Smith and Mrs. Neva A. Hesner, wife of C A. Hesner of Edgewood.
2 CONT Last September Mrs. Smith sustained injuries resulting from a fall (rest will not focus on viewer)
2 CONT
2 CONT Suggested edit: 
2 CONT Cynthia and Alonzo Smith came to Delaware County, Iowa, in 1863, not in 1848. Alonzo did his Civil War draft registration in New York on July 1, 1863. I guess after that, they then moved to Iowa. 
2 CONT Contributor: Squirrel (47213948)
