1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p3/2998/8460/53444836545b6941/Lyman_Wiswell_Gilmore_original.jpg?hash=9a0f29fe3245ce6746dae6d2f701eb1d6f71d66515274e3af69f5071731c95f8.1794038399
2 FORM jpg
2 _PRIM Y
2 NOTE Well, Katherine, part of this is true and part is not true. This picture is Lyman Wiswell Gilmore, Sr. It was his son, Lyman Wiswell Gilmore, Jr. who purportely flew before the Wright Brothers. Lyman Gilmore had the first commerci
3 CONC al airport in the United States at Grass Valley, California. There is no record of Lyman Gilmore Jr. ever having been in Hawaii. He did have several gold mines, one of which was called the Blue Nile. I do have a copy of his will i
3 CONC n my files. If you want to know more about Lyman Gilmore, Jr. I suggest that you do a google search for Lyman Gilmore. You will find quite a bit, even a Facebook site that has moving pictures of Lyman and his brother Charles proba
3 CONC bly done in the 1920,s. 
3 CONT
3 CONT One thing I have learned is that most family lore is mostly fiction with a few kernals of truth.
3 CONT
3 CONT It was not Sam who came to La Cresta, it was "Uncle Fred". And through my research I discovered that Uncle Fred had been married twice. It was Lyman Jr., Elmer and Charles who never married.  
2 NOTE As Aunt Sarah said, "Lyman had a plane up and flying in Idaho way before the Wright Brothers glew in North Carolina. He and his business partner flipped a silver dollar to decide who would fly the plane. His partner won the toss a
3 CONC nd flew the plane. The plane crashed and the partner was killed. Folks were quite angry and wanted to hang him for murder. He left Idaho and went to Grassvalley, CA. He was the first Navigator in California. He had pineappple plan
3 CONC tations in Hawaii. There was also a gold mine that Aunt Naomi mined in her later years.... Aunt Esther was the last person to see him when he was in the hospital before he died. He begged her not to cut his hair and she did. He di
3 CONC ed of pnemonia and all of his legacy and assest went missing.
3 CONT
3 CONT In the 1960's a public shool was dedicated to him in his memory. The National Enquirer(for what it was worth) published and circulated an article about this mystic multi-millionaire who drew pictures of the "bullet" trains came in
3 CONC to existence in Japan and Europe. The magazine article showed some of his drawings of many inventions that we use today. 
3 CONT
3 CONT Elmer Gilmore was another one of two brothers to Lymann and was a Violin Maker in Kooskey, Idaho, raised silver foxes, and lived in a tent. Elmer was born on April 6, 1875 and completed my violin on Tuesday, July 9th, 1946. When A
3 CONC unt Sarah Died on Dec. 7, 1980, the violin was willed to mein Aunt sarah's will plus her jewelry box and S& H Stamps. Presently I play iin a band called "Ruah," every Saturday evening. Now that Elmer the violin is electricfied, wh
3 CONC at a voice!  I have payed in a number of symphonies before my TBI experienced while serving in the Army Corps of Engineers in West Germany before the Berlin wall fell across Europe in 1989.  Found violin #19 in bichoffberger's Vio
3 CONC lin Shope in the Capitol Hill Area of Seattle, WA in 1984.  Needless to say I could not affort that price.  Grandpa Boogaards violin surfaced in the 1960's after Uncle Joe boogaard died.  This was the last time the entire family o
3 CONC f 9 sisters and one brother were united, sadly for Uncle Joe's funeral.  Father would not concent to have his children, Emily, Albert and Joe Jr. come to stay with us....
3 CONT
3 CONT Uncle Joe was a very successful business man with chicken ranching and loggiing in the Mount St. Helen's area and Spirit Lake until werehouser ran him off and he moved his family to Ketchikan, AK.  Where dad made his last port-of-
3 CONC call late June of 1986 and July.
3 CONT
3 CONT Sam last visited La Cresta, CA before some upsetting issues occured and Dad made sure he never came back!
3 CONT
3 CONT Sam was the last of three brothers, none of the brothers ever married. I guess women were in short supply those days in the west.
