1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In 1861 at Malahide Township (Div. 2, p. 16) is Sarah Whitesell, 30 born Canada West, a widow, with her daughter, “Mima”, 3. They are Epsic. Methodists living with her parents, Walter and Jemima Brown.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1871 at Malahide Township (Div. 4, p. 33) is John Teller, 48, a farmer of English origin, with wife Sarah, 39, of Scotch origin and their children, Walter, 6, John, 4, and “Violet”, 1. They are Baptists. Living with them is a b
2 CONC oarder, Elizabeth Windrow, 13. They are living next to the family of William and Mary Nickerbocker, and Joseph and Mary Graham.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1881 at Malahide Township (Div. 3, pp. 28 & 29) is John Teller, 57, a Farmer with wife, Sarah J., 48, and children, Walter, 17, John, 15, “Viletta” 11, and George A, 7. They are Baptists all born in Ontario. They live next to P
2 CONC eter Hoyle.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1891 at Malahide Township (Div. 3, p. 27) is John Teller, 68, a farmer, with wife, Sarah J., 58, and children, John, 26, single, Viola, 21, single and George A. S., 18, single. They are Baptists all born in Ontario. At [3-21] i
2 CONC s son Walter Teller, 27, farmer, single, a Methodist.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1901 at Malahide Township, Elgin County, (Div. 5, p. 12) is John Teller, 77, born 24 May 1823, a farmer, married to Sarah J., 69, born 27 Dec. 1831. They are Baptists. With them are children, Walter (T?), 37, born 24 Nov. 1863 
2 CONC and John (E?), 35, born 11 Sept. 1865 (or 1866?). They are farm laborers.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1901 County Directory gives John Teller, Gen Colin farming at Lot 21, Conc. 8 with sons, J. E. and Walter also farming there.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Edna Young Johnson’s memoirs:
2 CONT
2 CONT  Andrew Whitesell had a farm on the Jaffa road and he and Whitesell Sarah Jane (Brown);lived there and Ermina Mahala was born there. Andrew died when the daughter was a baby.” Sarah Jane went with her baby back home (Dunboyne) unt
2 CONC il she remarried again 4 years after and Ermina Mahala staid with her grandparents and Aunt Sally [Carter]. After Grandma Jemima died in 1878 and Grandpa Walter [Brown] died, Mother lived on with Aunt Sally until she [Aunt Sally] 
2 CONC died in 1881. Afterword Mother went to Windmill Point and Bertie among Carters. When Uncle George’s wife died Mina moved back to Dunboyne to help take care of George’s children.
2 CONT
2 CONT They [the Browns] owned most of the land between Aylmer and Port Bruce. My mother used to tell me which uncle owned which farm and I still remember. My grandmother, being a girl got nothing.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She [Sarah Jane] married George [I think this should be Andrew-George was Andrew’s brother] Whitesell who had a farm on the 4th concession [NW part of Lot 8] west of the Aylmer-Port Bruce road but when my mother was a year old he
2 CONC  died of tuberculosis and Sarah took her baby and went home to live. A couple of years later she remarried a widower with two sons. His name was John Teller ... My mother lived on with her grandparents and “Aunt Sally” till they d
2 CONC ied.”-
