2 CONT Page 1, The Medina County Gazette, Medina, Ohio, Friday, June 30th, 1922
2 CONT WERE MARRIED 60 YEARS AGO MONDAY
2 CONT Mr. and Mrs. John Phelps will celebrate their 60th wedding anniversary, tomorrow, July 1, 1922, at the home 419 E. Liberty St.m Medina, with a basket dinner to relatives and immediate friends and a reception to friends from 2 to 4
2 CONC p.m.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Phelps was born Feb. 15, 1842 in a log house at Brunswick, Mrs. Phelps was Emily Webster, and was born in Granger, July 6, 1845. They were married July 3, 1862. To this union we're born two children, a daughter, who died at th
2 CONC e age of seven years and one son, Jed C. Phelps, who lives with his aged parents at the present time.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. and Mrs. Phelps have spent their life in Brunswick and Medina, moving to Medina about 1p years ago. They have a host of friends who know them better as "Uncle John" and "Aunt Em", who wish them many more happy years of wedded 
2 CONC life together. Both are in fairly good health.
2 CONT
2 CONT State of Ohio Death Certificate
2 CONT John S. Phelps, Died: 16 February 1923, Medina, Medina County, Ohio, Male, White, Married, 81y0m1d, Born: 15 February 1842 Brunswick, Ohio, Teamster, Father: Julius C. Phelps, Born: CT, Mother: Roxie Phelps, Born: CT, Informant: M
2 CONC rs. Emma Phelps, Medina, Ohio, Burial: 18 Feb. 1923, Mt. Pleasant, Brunswick Tp.,O., Cause of Death: Arterio Sclerosis, File and. 12963.
