1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He enlisted and served as a substitute near the close of the "war of 1812" with England, and was a pensioner for many years.  He settled in Independence about 1821, when the western part of the State of New York wa
2 CONC s a wilderness; he was a justice of the peace twenty-eight years, supervisor for three years, and postmaster twenty years, and also a farmer. No children.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT He enlisted and served as a substitute near the close of the "war of 1812" with England, and was a pensioner for many years.  He settled in Independence about 1821, when the western part of the State of New York was a wilderness; 
2 CONC he was a justice of the peace twenty-eight years, supervisor for three years, and postmaster twenty years, and also a farmer. No children.
