1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nathan_Ames
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathan Ames (November 17, 1826 in Roxbury, New Hampshire – August 17, 1865 in Saugus, Massachusetts) was a patent solicitor who held the first patent in the United States for an escalator-like machine. The patent (#25,076) was gra
2 CONC nted on August 9, 1859, for an invention he called "Revolving Stairs". The escalator had steps mounted on a continuous belt or chain.  http://www.elevatorworld.com/blogs/be-it-known-i-invented-revolving-stairs/
2 CONT
2 CONT He also patented machines for improvement in polishing leather during the time when Lynn's shoe-making industry was one of the largest in the world. Another one of his patents was for a polygraph, an early copying machine that ope
2 CONC rated by using pens connected by wires. Another patent he held was for an improved grater.
2 CONT
2 CONT A writer and a poet, Ames has a disquisition and a Class Ode published during his time at Harvard. His book of poetry Pirate’s Glen and Dungeon Rock was published in 1853. These poems were based the local pirate legend of Dungeon 
2 CONC Rock.
2 CONT
2 CONT His brother Joseph was an American portrait artist.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ames was educated at Phillips Academy at Andover, and Harvard College.
