1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Daily Times, Dubuque, Iowa
2 CONT Wednesday 06 Oct 1897
2 CONT Wales Smith, a prominent citizen of Greeley, Iowa, went out hunting squirels last Thursday and had his gun directly in front of him, waiting to get a shot at a squirrel, when both barrels were accidentally discharged, the stock of
2 CONC  the gun striking him in the addomen as the result of the recoil.  He felt that he was painfully hurt, but did not believe that anything very serious had happened until he found that the local physician was unable to give him any 
2 CONC relief.  Then he sent for Dr. Allen Staples of this city who went out Monday to see him.  He gives it as his opinion that the bowels are ruptured, and that Mr. Smith cannot live.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daily Times, Dubuque, Iowa 
2 CONT Friday 08 Oct 1897
2 CONT Wales Smith, the young farmer living near Edgewood, and who was severely injuired from the kick of a gun while hunting squirrels, has since died, the funeral occuring Wednesday.  His brother tells us that while holding the gun in 
2 CONC front of him both barrels were discharged, the recoil being so severe as to cause death as state by Dr. Staples.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/5900386/wales-t-smith Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com
