1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=10901097
2 CONT
2 CONT From findagrave: Mary Tubbs was the daughter of Caleb Colvin and Jane Eliza (Harris) Tubbs. She was a sister to Charles and Silas Tubbs. She was married first to Charles McGrath. She then married Cyrus Monroe Packard, and later Jo
2 CONC hn Wagner. Mary had no children.
2 CONT ---------------------
2 CONT Last Will and Testament Filed:Sept. 18, 1918 Record: Will of Record No. 4, Page 265 Petition for Probate of Will filed Sept. 18, 1918 states that Mary Wagner died at Cedar Township, Mitchell County, Iowa on September 6th, 1918, le
2 CONC aving a last Will and Testament and asking that said last Will and Testament be admitted to probate and recorded in Mitchell County Iowa. Petition also asks that J.R. Lonie be appointed Administrator with Will annexed of said Esta
2 CONC te without bonds. Notice of proof of Will published in the Mitchell County Press and Osage Journal, a weekly newspaper printed at Osage, Mitchell County Iowa, for three consecutive weeks, the date of the last publication filed Oct
2 CONC . 9th , 1918 and proof of such publication filed Oct. 12, 1918 by affidavit of H.C. Hill, Publisher. On Dec. 10, 1918, by order of the District Court of Mitchell County Iowa, said Will is admitted to probate and record in Mitchell
2 CONC  County Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Copy of Will as follows:--
2 CONT
2 CONT "In the name of God, Amen, I Mary Wagner, of the County of Mitchell in the state of Iowa, being weak in body and in sound mind, memory, and understanding, but considering the uncertainty of life, do make and publish this, my last 
2 CONC will and testament in the manner and form following, To wit: all my Real Estate, money and credits of which I am possessed, I will and bequeath to my loving husband John Wagner, during his life and upon his decease to Josie Tubbs 
2 CONC and Jessie Tubbs of Mitchell County Iowa, to each have Five Hundred Dollars. Her mark, Mary Wagner Witness to mark: E. Mae Lonie
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnesses: M.A. Hansen L.W. Knoulton Dated Sept. 1st, 1918
