2 CONT From findagrave: Silas G. Tubbs obituary
2 CONT
2 CONT The Funeral of Silas G. Tubbs occurred Monday at Mitchell at the Methodist Church, but as he was a resident of this place until a short time ago we take the liberty to mention this in our letter. He and his family resided here unt
2 CONC il the death of his wife, which occurred last July. Soon after this he went to Sherburn Minnesota and about a month ago to the pineries in Itasca where on the nineteenth of this month he lost his life by being struck by a falling 
2 CONC log, dieing in a few days. He leaves two little children, a mother, brother, and sister to mourn his loss. They have the sympathy of all in their bereavement.
2 CONT
2 CONT Osage, Mitchell County Iowa, February 27 1896
2 CONT ----------------------------------
2 CONT West Mitchell Obituary of Silas G. Tubbs
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral of Silas Tubbs, whose death occurred in the pineries of northern Minnesota, was held inthe M.E. church Monday morning. While at work near a large pile of logs, one slipped and struck him causing his death a few hours l
2 CONC ater. He leaves two children, one about five years of age and the other about seven.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mitchell Co. Press, Osage Iowa Thursday February 27, 1896
2 CONT
2 CONT Transcribed by Kathy Pike 
