1 NOTE {geni:about_me} First Methodist Episcopal Church, Rochester, N. Y.,  June 30, 1896. Rev. Melville R. Webster, D. D. Pastor.  B. S. SWETLAND, Sec'y, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dear Sir: — My great grandmother was Mercy  Swetland, who married Ashbell Webster and both died  at Cuba, N. Y. I visited Connecticut this summer and  made the following notes: In 1762 Joseph Swetland  sells land to Elija Beck of 
2 CONC Middletown. Joseph Swet-  land, from love and other sufficient reasons gives his son  Israel Swetland 26 acres five miles from the Bolton line.  In 1777, John and Abbey of Summers, Mass., buys land  in East Hartford, Conn. In 1778
2 CONC  Benjamin and Sarah  Swetland sell land. In 1772 Joseph and Daniel Swet-  land are mentioned. In 1805 Sarah Swetland, a widow,  aged 83 died. Niel Swetland marries Abigal, daughter  of Jason Webster. Mercy Swetland had brothers na
2 CONC med  Ira and Silas and half brothers Eleazer and Eli. Palta  was a cousin of Mercy and married Maria, a daughter of  Ira Swetland. Ira died April 1st, 1856, aged 75 years;  and Ruth August 14, 1844, aged 65. Sanford Swetland,  bor
2 CONC n at Longmeadow, Mass., Oct. 12, 1823, died at Port-  land, N. Y., May 31, 1884. These are random notes but  Longmeadows and East Longmeadows and Summers are  not far apart and doubtless the Swetlands in these places  were closely
2 CONC  related. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Fraternally yours, 
2 CONT
2 CONT M. R. Webster
