1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Roland recalls while quite young visiting "uncle Orrin" near Buffalo NY, where he worked in the Packard plant, making wooden spoke wheels.  He recalls going for ride on the Niagra river in Orrin's motor launch. Lat
2 CONC er in life, Orrin spent winters in Florida picking fruit, and his mother Lena was sent south to him in her later years to escape northern weather.
2 CONT
2 CONT Orrin married Bertha Nagel. They had two children; Janet and Orrin Leroy the 3rd.
