2 DATE 22 APR 1859
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lancaster
3 STAE Wisconsin
3 CTRY United States
1 BURI
2 DATE AFT 30 JUL 1950
2 PLAC Rialto Park Cemetery (Plot: Section N Block 01 Plot 02 SubPlot A), Rialto, San Bernardino County, California USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 30 JUL 1950
2 ADDR
3 STAE California
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Death Claims Lucy Humphrey Pioneer Resident of Rialto
2 CONT
2 CONT RIALTO, July 31 Mrs. Lucy E. Humphrey, 91, widely known Rialto pioneer and a charter monr ber of the Rialto Women's Bene. fit association, died Sunday in a San Bernardino hospital. Mrs. Humphrey was a native of Lancaster, Wis. She
2 CONC  had lived in Rialto 62 years and was also a member of the Maccabees. Mrs. Humphrey was the widow of W. D. Humphrey, who was well known in Rialto as a contractor and tradesman. Their old home was on Olive street at First street op
2 CONC posite the Congregational church. Mr. Humphrey died 26 years ago. Surviving are three daughters, Mrs. Carl Head, Venice; Mrs. Howard E. Wilkerson, Bakersfield; and Mrs. Delbert V. Stewart, Rialto; two sons, W. D. Humphrey, Lakepor
2 CONC t, California; and Earl D. Humphrey, Honolulu; five grandchildren; and seven great-grandchildren. Funeral services will be held Wednesday at 3:30 p.m. at the Mark B. Shaw Memorial chapel in San Bernardino. Interment will be in Ria
2 CONC lto Park cemetery. It has been requested that all ladies of the Rialto Review of the Women's Benefit association meet in a body at the funeral chapel prior to the services. The W.B.A. will have a part in the services.
2 CONT
2 CONT August 1, 1950 The San Bernardino County Sun from San Bernardino, California · Page 15
2 CONT **************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT When Lucy Ella Thurstin was born on April 22, 1859, in Grant County, Wisconsin, her father, David, was 36 and her mother, Sarah, was 30. She had three sons and Four daughters with William David Humphrey between 1881 and 1896. She 
2 CONC died on July 30, 1950, in San Bernardino, California, at the age of 91, and was buried in Rialto, California.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lester P. Humphrey 1881–1940 Callie L Humphrey 1886– William D Humphrey 1887–1956 Laura C. Humphrey 1892–1979 (Married Delbert Stewart) Leota L Humphrey 1896–1985 (Married Howard Wilkerson) Earl Humphrey -  Maude Humphrey - (Marri
2 CONC ed Carl Head)
