1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Information about Charles Henry Leete's later life, death, and burial were obtained from the foreward of "Potsdupinni: A History of Potsdam, New York", written by Charles H. Leete and published by his son, Edward
2 CONC  Leete in Hartsdale, NY, August 1967.  
2 CONT * A paper copy of "Potsdupinni: A History of Potsdam, New York" is in the possession of Daniel Parker of Potsdam, NY as of February 26, 2023.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * Charles' birth, professional, and death information are available in his obituary in ''The New York Times'', Thursday, January 9, 1936, page 21. He was former headmaster of the Leete School for Girls. "Dr. Leete, holder of a Doc
2 CONC torate of Philosophy from the University of Leipzig, traced his ancestry back to the back of William the Conqueror. His first American forebear came here from England in 1639. Among the prominent Leets od colonial days was William
2 CONC  Leete, Governor of the New Haven Colony from 1658 to 1683."
2 CONT * From https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/79457837/charles-henry-leete:
2 CONT ** "Charles earned his Bachelor's degree at Yale University in 1879, after which he went to Leipzig, where he earned his Master's degree, and then, in 1890, his Ph.D. He devoted his life to study.
2 CONT ** "After teaching for several years in Potsdam, New York, he became the State Normal and Training School President in Potsdam. He was known as the Historian of Northern New York and made a complete study of the geography and geol
2 CONC ogical formations of that country and its people. 
2 CONT ** "Among others, his papers on the Early History of Potsdam, Some Landmarks of Potsdam, A Study in Geographic Names, and The St. Lawrence Ten Towns, printed in the Potsdam Herald-Record, are invaluable for the historical data the
2 CONC y contain, which represents a vast amount of research. 
2 CONT ** "His advice and assistance during the compilation of the Leete genealogy for the 1934 edition of the book ''THE DESCENDANTS OF WILLIAM LEETE'' were very helpful.
2 CONT ** "As a widow, he continued to live in Potsdam but spent the winter months with his son at Hartsdale, New York."
2 CONT * Charles wrote, and published, these books:
2 CONT ** Leete, Charles Henry, ''Exercises in Geography'' (Longmans, Green, and co., 1902).
2 CONT ** Leete, Charles Henry and George Goudie Chisholm, ''Longman's School Geography'' (Longmans, Green and Co., 1897).
2 CONT ** Leete, Charles Henry, ''School Geography'' (Longmans, Green, and Co., 1890).
