2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Abt  1941 ?
2 _PRIM Y
2 NOTE Grand Mother made the 9 girls and one boy walk to Castle Rock down the mountain five miles one way to Church.  She was a devout bible believing Christian Woman.  She put up with a lot from her husband.  She was a logger, she remov
3 CONC ed many of the trees from around 131 South Silver Lake Road, Castle Rock WA.  Aunt Sarah, Aunt Esther, and Aunt Edna partnered to purchase what land was left.  Grand Father would not complete the registration to own the 400 acres.
3 CONC   Leslie and Uncle Joe purchased the part and parcel.  Wherehauser ran Uncle Joe off to Alaska in the late 1950's and early 1960's.
3 CONT
3 CONT She would allow Mama to burn the kerosine oil lamp well into the night so she could have the opportunity to do well in school and she did.  Anna Carnine, a Cousin, taught Mama how to play the piano and drums.  When Anna Carnine di
3 CONC ed, Cousine Jeanne called us to come and receive what she wanted us to have.  
3 CONT
3 CONT Grand Mother's prayers were answered one day....Grand Father had a dream that the Devil came to take him to hell.  Naturally he did not want to go and was fighting with the Devil.  He decided to give his life to Christ instead and
3 CONC  quit drinking.  From that night on, he never drank a drop.  This story was shared with me by Aunt Sarah and Aunt Edna.
