2 CONT Elmira NY Star Gazette 1936 
2 CONT
2 CONT MRS. MALINDA ANGELL 
2 CONT Knoxville—Mrs. Malinda Smith 
2 CONT Angell died Saturday, Apr. 25, 1936, 
2 CONT after an illness of four weeks. The 
2 CONT funeral was held at the home on 
2 CONT North Wate r Street Monday at 2 
2 CONT p. m., the Rev. Howard L. Spangler 
2 CONT officiating. Burial was in Riverside 
2 CONT Cemetery. Pall Bearers were E. H. 
2 CONT Gilbert, C. E. Wainwright, W. E. 
2 CONT Jones and R. H. Edgcomb. 
2 CONT Mrs. Angell, the daughte r of 
2 CONT Caleb and Susan Bowen Smith, was 
2 CONT born in Deerfleld Township, Mar. 
2 CONT 12, 1853. On Jan . 1, 1873 she married Edwar d Angell, now deceased
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Corning NY Evening Leader 1936
2 CONT MRS. MALINDA ANGELL 
2 CONT KNOXVILLE, Pa. — Mrs. Maiinda Angell, 83. of Knoxville. died 
2 CONT at her home on North Water street 
2 CONT j Saturday noon April 25th, 1936, 
2 CONT I after an illness of several weeks. 
2 CONT Funeral services were held ths 
2 CONT 'afternoon at 2 o'clock at ;he 
2 CONT home, the Rev. Howard . Spangj ler officiating, with burial in Riverside Cemetery, Knoxville. 
2 CONT Mrs. Angell was the widow of 
2 CONT j Edward Angell who died many 
2 CONT [years sgo. Surviving are three 
2 CONT | daughters, Mrs. Alta Beaty of New 
2 CONT 'Berlin, N. Y.. Mrs. Rena Bull of 
2 CONT i New York City and Mrs. Cynthia 
2 CONT Angell of Rochester. N. Y., and 
2 CONT several grandchildren.
