1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://bycommonconsent.com/2007/09/12/william-henry-harrison-sagers-a-brief-history/
2 CONT
2 CONT Harriet Emmeline Barney Sagers Young was born in Amhest, Ohio on October 13, 1830 the daughter of Royal Baney and Sarah Esterbrook. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married William Henry Harrison Sagers. He was also married polygamously to other wives at the time. Arriving in Utah, the family settled in Tooele, Utah. In 1856, Harriet (the ‘oldest’ of the Sagers wives at the time) married 
2 CONC Brigham Young, after, one assumes, she was divorced from Sagers. Young had Sagers’ children sealed to him. She and Brigham Young had one child.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harriet died at the age of 80 on February 14, 1911 in Salt Lake City, Utah.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Daughter of Royal Barney, Jr. and Sarah Bowen Estabrook
2 CONT
2 CONT Married William Henry Harrison Sagers, Mar 1846, Leroy Twp., Genessee, New York, later divorced
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Brigham Young, 14 Mar 1856, Salt Lake City, Salt Lake, Utah
2 CONT
2 CONT Children - Infant Young, Phineas Howe Young, Mary Lola Sagers Young, Royal Barney Sagers Young, Sarah Emeline Young, Joseph Ormal Sagers Young, Mary Sagers Young
2 CONT
2 CONT History - Harriet embraced the Mormon doctrine in connection with the rest of her father's family in the early days of the Church, and accepted all the principles thereof. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Harriet was tall and stately in appearance, of fair complexion, and had finely formed features. After an acquaintance with Brigham Young, she recognized in him qualities of a good husband and was married to him March 14, 1856. She
2 CONC  was the mother of five children, three sons and two daughters, four of her children by her first marriage.
2 CONT * Updated from [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=24641363 Find A Grave Memorial] via mother [http://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000030576890107 Sarah Bowen  Barney (born Estabrook)] by [http://www.geni.
2 CONC com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 5 2015, 4:13:32 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Daughter of Royal Barney, Jr. and Sarah Bowen Estabrook
2 CONT
2 CONT Married William Henry Harrison Sagers, March 1846, Leroy Twp., Genessee, New York, later divorced
2 CONT
2 CONT Children - Royal Barney Sagers Young, Sarah Emeline Young, Joseph Ormal Sagers Young, Mary Lola Sagers Young
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Brigham Young, 14 Mar 1856, Salt Lake City, Salt Lake, Utah
2 CONT
2 CONT Children - infant Young, Phineas Howe Young
2 CONT
2 CONT History - Harriet embraced the Gospel in connection with the rest of her father's family in the early days of the Church, and accepted all the principles thereof. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Harriet was tall and stately in appearance, of fair complexion, and had finely formed features. After an acquaintance with Brigham Young, she recognized in him qualities of a good husband and was married to him March 14, 1856. She
2 CONC  was the mother of five children, three sons and two daughters, four of her children by her first marriage.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://old.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=24641363 Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 5 2018, 10:58:39 UTC''
