1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A RECOLLECTION BY DOUGLAS KNOWLTON: On one visit to Charles Sawyer, I remember a bald man with a rather damaged looking head and face. It was explained that the man had been an architect and had incurred the wrath 
2 CONC of a bricklayer years before. One day when this architect was visitng a construction site for a mutli-story building, the bricklayer had upended a wheel barrow full of bricks on this man who was standing below. He survived, but wi
2 CONC th greatly diminished capacities. He did not join in the general conversation except too answer questions put to him directly. His replies were all mono-syllabic, grabled and accompanied by hearty laughter. I often visited Uncle C
2 CONC harles' office. I associate him with the City Government. He was an architect, maybe the architect for the city of san Francisco. 
