1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/104145328/harvey_guy-garrett
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth Name: Guy
2 CONT Died in a Hinton Hospital
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Marriage, Names as on record==
2 CONT Groom: Harvey Guy Garrett, Age 21
2 CONT ~
2 CONT Bride: Cordelia May Bragg, Age 21
2 CONT Memorial #: 104143815
2 CONT Married: 5-5-1924, W.Va., Raleigh Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Parents, Names as on record==
2 CONT Bride: Cora Harris, Age 23
2 CONT b: W.Va., Putnam Co.
2 CONT ~
2 CONT Groom: Charles L. Garrett, Age 21
2 CONT b: W.Va., Jackson Co.
2 CONT Married: 6-25-1900, W.Va., Jackson Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Obituary==
2 CONT Headline: Funeral Set For Garrett
2 CONT Newspaper: Register and Post Herald
2 CONT Published: Sat., March 29, 1975
2 CONT Location: Page 7, Column 6
2 CONT Reads:
2 CONT SANDSTONE (RNS) — Harvey Guy Garrett, 72, died Friday morning in a Hinton hospital after a short illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born May 29, 1902, at Ripley, he as a son of the late Charles and Cora Harrison Garrett.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had lived in Raleigh County for the past 52 years and was a retired coal miner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include his wife, Cordelia Bragg Garrett; one son, Edward of Rising Sun. Md.; four daughters, Mrs. Helen Fleshman of Rainelle, Mrs. Elizabeth Gwinn of Bellwood, Mrs. Lucille Baillis of Akron. Ohio, and Mrs. Joann Bragg o
2 CONC f Jumping Branch; one sister. Mrs. Fay Bragg of Akron , Ohio; 17 grandchildren and 5 greatgrandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be at 2 p.m. Sunday at Ronald Meadows Funeral Home in Hinton with Rev. C. C. Corker in charge. Burial will be in the family cemetery at Sandstone.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends may call from 5-9 p.m. today.
2 CONT ~ ~
2 CONT Obit Courtesy of: Russell E. Bennett, Jr.,
2 CONT Find-a-grave Contributor #: 46934630
2 CONT Thank You.
2 CONT ~ ~
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Summers Cemetery Clarity==
2 CONT Obit listed burial place as 'Family Cemetery' which back then meant the Bragg burial place.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Cemetery Continued==
2 CONT The Bragg Cemetery (Falls View Lane off New River Road) is directly in the rear of, and adjacent to, the Richmond Cemetery in Sandstone. There was some kind of a dispute between the Richmond's and the Bragg's, so they buried the B
2 CONC ragg's just outside the fence. You can literally jump over the fence and land on a grave on the other side its that close. A lot of old Obits and Death certificates called the Bragg Cemetery the Richmond Graveyard. The cemeteries 
2 CONC are literally across the river from Sandstone. There used to be a Ferry at Sandstone that took the residents back and forth from the Raleigh side to Sandstone and vice versa. All of these Raleigh folks got their mail at Sandstone,
2 CONC  their groceries and dry goods, and they caught the train there. Everything involved around Sandstone so a lot of these folks were said to live in Sandstone, Summers Co., even though they were on the Raleigh side.
2 CONT ~ ~
