1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=10945721
2 CONT
2 CONT From findagrave: Mrs. Isaac Parr, 70, Dies After a Brief Illness Wednesday
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held last Friday for Mrs. Isaac Parr, 70, who died Aug. 15 at Mitchell Memorial Hospital in Osage. She was stricken at their home and was taken to the hospital, dying of a heart attack the same day. The Rev. 
2 CONC Robert E. Leverenz, pastor of the Methodist Church Riceville, was in charge of the services at the Champion Funeral Home. Burial was made in the Osage Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jessie Edna Tubbs was born Mar. 20, 1892 at Sherburn, Minn, the daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Silas Tubbs. After the death of her parents when she was 2 years old, she lived with her uncle and aunt, Mr. and Mrs. Charles Tubbs. She was 
2 CONC married to Isaac Parr Dec. 24 1919. Osage has always been their home. Mr. Parr served as a rural mail carrier 41 years. She was baptized and became a member of the Methodist Church when she was a young girl at Mitchell. She had be
2 CONC en an active member of the church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are her husband, Isaac of Osage, four children. Ernest of Riceville; Kenneth of Joliet, Ill; Mrs. Emil Tonn of Reinbeck; Mrs. Willis Mouw of St. Ansgar; two sisters, Mrs. Perry Galley of Kenyon, Minn; Mrs. Ernest Coonrad
2 CONC t of Waverly; three brothers, Ray, and Earl Tubbs of Osage; Clayton Tubbs of Floyd, and 10 grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Osage News August 1962
2 CONT
2 CONT Added notes by Kathy Pike: 1. Ernest Parr is Isaac Ernest Parr, known as "Junior" Parr 2. Mrs. Emil Tonn is Virginia (Parr) Tonn 3. Mrs. Willis Mouw is Betty (Parr) Mouw 4. Mrs. Perry Galley is Josie (Tubbs) Galley 5. Mrs. Ernest 
2 CONC Coonradt is Ruth (Tubbs) Coonradt 6. Jessie was actually 3 1/2 years old when her parents died and she went to live with her aunt and uncle Charles and Ruth Tubbs. 7. Jessie died August 15, 1962
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT Jessie was the daughter of Silas and Martha (Packard) Tubbs but was raised by her uncle and aunt, Charles and Ruth (Clark) Tubbs after the death of her parents. She was the wife of Ernest "Ike" Parr and the mother of Ernest "Junio
2 CONC r", Kenneth, Virginia, and Bette. 
