1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.legacy.com/obituaries/timesunion-albany/obituary.aspx?n=jane-k-jamison&pid=3583957&fhid=2145
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane K. Jamison, 75, died Tuesday, May 24, 2005 at Our Lady of Mercy Life Center, Guilderland. She was born in Chicago, Ill., the daughter of the late Howard and Frances Brooks Keeler. Jane was a graduate of Francis Parker Academy
2 CONC , Chicago and Denison University, Granville, Ohio. She was a member of Alpha Omega Pi Sorority. Mrs. Jamison received her B.S. in nursing at the University of Michigan, Ann Arbor, Mich., 1952. Jane was a nurse at Ellis Hospital, S
2 CONC chenectady. She was a member of Grace Baptist Church, Guilderland and loved to vacation in Cape Cod. She also loved her cats, Calvin and Hobbs, and was an avid bridge player. Jane was the wife of the late Robert W. Jamison and is 
2 CONC survived by two daughters, Linda (Jim) Rose of Guilderland and Carol (Mike) McTague of Averill Park; grandmother of Brian, Steven and Kathleen Rose and Sarah McTague; aunt of George Jamison III and Ruth J. Berkery. Funeral service
2 CONC  will be Sunday 2 p.m. at the Grace Baptist Church, 5958 State Farm Road, Guilderland, NY 12084. Relatives and friends are also invited to call Saturday 4 to 7 p.m. at the Tebbutt Funeral Home, 633 Central Ave., Albany. Those who 
2 CONC wish make make donations to the Community Hospice of Albany, 445 New Karner Road, Albany, NY 12205 or Community Care Givers, Inc., 300 Millrose Court, Guilderland, NY 12084. 
