1 OCCU New York state banking official
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Edward's age when he got married [and thus his estimated year of birth], his occupation, and his place of birth are available at https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:939Z-1CGR-1?view=index&action=view
2 CONT * Edward's birth and death information are available at https://www.myheritage.com/matchingresult-181149fb6d76717d734370240ef63f4e?auth=3e5ef317b07f311ef072264285b5c11f&callback_token=52CQx6ed9k0wfKQsMiCIsO8TLZgv0yzFkxvxhakN&trn=p
2 CONC artner_Geni&trp=match_button_profile#smart_matches
2 CONT * Edward and Helen were married on 1 July 1922 in Hillcrest, near the Village of Hobart, Town of Stamford, Delaware County, New York. See the ''Watertown Daily Times'', Wednesday Afternoon, July 5, 1922, page eighteen.
2 CONT * On 18 July 1924, Edward was named a national bank examiner. "He began his duties this week, being assigned to the lower New York district, which embraces Long Island, New York City, and the lower Hudson Valley. Mr. Leete is a gr
2 CONC aduate of the Normal High School [of Potsdam, N.Y.] in 1911 and of Yale in 1916. He spent a year at Columbia Law School and for several years was with the Chase National Bank." See the ''Watertown Daily Times'', Friday Afternoon, 
2 CONC July 18, 1924, page three.
2 CONT * On 15 November 1941, Edward was "certified by the State Civil Service Commission as being the candidate who was first on a list of nine candidates who passed a professional examination held May 24 for appointment to the position
2 CONC  of Deputy Superintendent of Banks, salary $8,500 to $12,000." See ''The Daily Argus'', Mount Vernon, N.Y., Saturday, November 15, 1941, page 4.
2 CONT * On 21 November 1941 in Albany, New York, Edward was appointed as Deputy Superintendent of Banks for the State of New York. See the ''Buffalo Evening News'', Friday, November 21, 1941, page 40.  
