1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Ezra Weston Loomis Pound''' (30 October 1885 – 1 November 1972) was an American expatriate poet and critic and a major figure in the early modernist movement in poetry. He became known for his role in developing
2 CONC  Imagism, which, in reaction to the Victorian and Georgian poets, favored tight language, unadorned imagery, and a strong correspondence between the verbal and musical qualities of the verse and the mood it expressed. His best-kno
2 CONC wn works include Ripostes (1912), Hugh Selwyn Mauberley (1920), and his unfinished 120-section epic, The Cantos, which consumed his middle and late career, and was published between 1917 and 1969.
2 CONT
2 CONT More...[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ezra_Pound Wiki - Ezra Pound]
