2 TITL Graduation Photo 1936
2 _PRIM Y
2 NOTE Mom was the top honor graduate in her Highschool in 1936.  She played the piano and th drums, A.K.A. the drums.  Granmther Olive Marie Gray boogaard would allow her to study and burn the kerosine lamps so she could get good grades
3 CONC .  She also did not have the heavy work that the other 8 sisters and one brother were tasked with.  She alswys had a love for learning.  In 1968 she went to Olympic College to enter the "LEGGS" Program.  Like manywomen in that tim
3 CONC e had children and were married to working men.  She was one of the fist women to earn her Associates in Arts and Sciences.  She frmly believed in the Head Start Program and the Montessori Methods and Theory in Education.  She als
3 CONC o participated in High School Journalism like Dad.  Hw dida young lady from Castle Rock, WA meet a fine young man from New Orleans, LA?  WWII!  World War II caused the mobilization of the Amerian population like no other war in Un
3 CONC ited States History.  By trains the young men who signed their enlistment papers were processed and moved to their training camps.  Dad met Mother in San Diego, CA.  Aunt Ester invited the young dashing and fine Marine to one of h
3 CONC er parties.  Mother would also swim out to the ships in the San Diego Harbor.  She moved to San Diego, CA to enter through the Door of Hope and become one of many young women who would become a Nurse in a Catholic Hospital, Mercy 
3 CONC Hospital, San Diego, CA.  Now we knowthe rest of the story....
